Hi,

...suggest to open the shapefile in ArcView or ArcGIS, and export data
from there into txt or other formats you need (mind the units of the
projection).

This then could go into your GPS (as the main application to guide
pilots/captains, surveyors, let's say).

I stretch the KML KMZ format for this with Google Earth applications!!
Fascinating.

I agree that all of this is not really super straightforward, but it's
robust and allows for reaching goals. GIS people will have no problem with
the steps outlined.

Thank goodness, Distance Sampling provides us with such a great spatial
survey design tool!!

Very best
  F.

