15, A =3D=20
194375000, L=3D1812262.=20=20
Thus est(N)should be (181*.0063315*1.7008*194375000)/(2*1812262) =3D 104.=
5268
But DISTANCE reports the est(N) =3D 105.00

Further, DISTANCE reports the est(density) =3D 0.0053775 which agrees wit=
h=20

my hand calculation, but does nor agree with the abundance estimate from=20=

DISTANCE.

I am going to be calculating abundance estimates by hand for my final=20
analysis, because I have temporal strata (seasons within years), but I=20=

need to pool surveys over the all temporal strata to fit the detection=20=

functions, due to sample size restrictions.

That brings up a second question - can I use post-stratification to get=20=

DISTANCE to calculate the abundance estimates within temporal strata,=20
while pooling all of the data across seasons to fit the detection=20
functions?  I tried using post-stratification by temporal strata (season-=

year), but DISTANCE wasn't using the line lengths for the temporal=20
strata.  Instaed, within each strata, it used the entire line length and=20=

thus came up with an incorrect abundance estimate.  I can't figure out ho=
w=20
to make it use the correct totals for line length within the temporal=20
strata.

